apogee chat: --input-format stream-json cannot be combined with --output-format text; a driven chat session speaks the protocol in both directions
=== apogee chat --graph code
--- stdin
hi
--- exit 1
--- stdout
--- stderr
apogee chat: --graph applies to the --attach given with it -- for every attach, set attachments.graph in the config; for one, /attach <path> --graph=code|off
=== apogee chat --allow write_file
--- stdin
hi
--- exit 1
--- stdout
--- stderr
apogee chat: --allow, --deny and --allow-host need --tools: without tools, nothing is asked
=== apogee chat --tools --allow nothing
--- stdin
hi
--- exit 1
--- stdout
--- stderr
apogee chat: --allow: 'nothing' is not a tool this chat asks about -- the ones it asks about: delete_file, delete_note, edit_file, run_command, write_file, write_note (a website takes --allow-host)
