=== apogee chat --help
--- stdin
--- exit 0
--- stdout
Start or resume an interactive conversation
Usage: apogee chat [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -h,--help                   Print this help message and exit
  -m,--model BACKEND          Backend or model to use
  -s,--system TEXT            System prompt for the session
  --rag COLLECTION            Retrieve context from this collection each turn (see 'apogee embed'); "" switches off the config's auto_rag for this session
  --rag-limit INT             How many chunks to inject (default 4)
  --retriever TEXT:{lexical,vector,hybrid,auto}
                              How to search the collection: lexical, vector, hybrid, or auto
  --rerank BACKEND            Backend that reorders retrieved chunks with one generation call, on (the utility model), or off
  --image PATH ...            An image to attach, as /attach does: seen as it is with the first message by a model that can, described for one that cannot (repeatable)
  --attach PATH ...           A file, folder or glob to attach to the chat: indexed, inlined when it fits, retrieved each turn when not (repeatable)
  --graph TEXT:{code,off}     For the --attach given here: code builds a folder's code graph, off indexes its chunks alone (default: the config's attachments.graph, else code)
  -t,--temperature FLOAT      Sampling temperature
  -n,--max-tokens INT         Maximum tokens per reply
  --think TEXT:{on,off,auto}  Whether a reasoning model thinks first: on, off, or auto (per question)
  --no-recall                 Recall no earlier chats in this run
  --allow TOOL                Allow a tool for this chat without asking (repeatable, with --tools)
  --deny TOOL                 Refuse a tool or website for this chat without asking (repeatable)
  --allow-host TEXT           Allow fetching from a website for this chat without asking (repeatable)
  --think-budget INT:INT in [0 - 1000000]
                              The most tokens a reasoning model may think for before it answers
  --tools                     Let the model call tools
  --search                    Enable the provider's server-side web search
  --no-color                  Disable ANSI colour output
  --raw                       Show answers' Markdown as written instead of rendering it on the terminal
  --output-format TEXT:{text,stream-json}
                              Output format: text (default) or stream-json for a machine driver
  --input-format TEXT:{text,stream-json}
                              Input format: text (default) or stream-json; follows --output-format if unset
  -v,--verbose                Print progress notes
  --resume CHAT               Resume a saved conversation by id or name
  --suite MODEL_SUITE_OR_OFF  Run under this suite -- its members answer for the roles it names -- or off for none
  --warm                      Load the suite's members now, on the progress line, rather than at first use
  --force                     Run the suite even when what it takes is over this machine's memory
  -q,--quiet                  No progress line while the suite's members load
  -c,--continue               Resume the most recent conversation
  --branch GIT_REF            Branch under review for the git tools (the head); never checked out
  --base GIT_REF              Ref to compare against (default: the default branch)
  --remote REMOTE             Remote to resolve refs against (default origin)
  --fetch                     Always fetch the refs before diffing
  --no-fetch                  Never fetch; refuse a ref that is absent
--- stderr
